  "articleBody": "Repairing a rental property often comes with a tight schedule and budget, but making certain mistakes can really derail your efforts. One frequent error is *not budgeting for hidden damage*. What looks like a simple fix on the surface might hide deeper issues that will add to your costs. Always factor in a contingency. Another big one is *failing to inspect all systems* before starting work. You might fix one problem only to have another immediately pop up, leading to more downtime. Do a thorough inspection first! *Skipping permits* when they're required for electrical, plumbing, or structural changes is a definite no-no and can lead to fines or re-work. Finally, *delaying major-system repairs* while spending on cosmetic items first is a common pitfall. Always address critical safety and habitability issues before focusing on aesthetics. When in doubt, especially for complex or critical repairs, bringing in a licensed professional can help you avoid these costly missteps and ensure the work is done right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
